examples.question_text:
The trapezium has area $84$ cm$^2$. Its parallel sides are $a=9$ cm and $b$ cm, and its perpendicular height is $h=7$ cm. Use $A=\frac12h(a+b)$ to find $b$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.5,0);
\coordinate (C) at (3.5,2);
\coordinate (D) at (0.8,2);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (0.8,0)--(D);
\draw (0.8,0.18)--(0.98,0.18)--(0.98,0);
\path (2.15,2) node[above] {$a$};
\path (2.25,0) node[below] {$b$};
\path (0.8,1) node[right] {$h$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
$\begin{align*}A&=\frac12h(a+b)\\84&=\frac12(7)(9+b)\\84&=3.5(9+b)\\24&=9+b\\b&=15\text{ cm}\end{align*}$
Divide by $3.5$, then subtract $9$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.5,0);
\coordinate (C) at (3.5,2);
\coordinate (D) at (0.8,2);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (0.8,0)--(D);
\draw (0.8,0.18)--(0.98,0.18)--(0.98,0);
\path (2.15,2) node[above] {$9\text{ cm}$};
\path (2.25,0) node[below,text={rgb,255:red,38;green,140;blue,255}] {$b=15\text{ cm}$};
\path (0.8,1) node[right] {$7\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.question_text:
The hexagon has perimeter $P=3a+3b$. Find $a$ when $P=42$ cm and $b=5$ cm.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (-1.2,1.1);
\coordinate (B) at (1.2,1.1);
\coordinate (C) at (1.9,0);
\coordinate (D) at (0.9,-1.6);
\coordinate (E) at (-0.9,-1.6);
\coordinate (F) at (-1.9,0);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--(E)--(F)--cycle;
\path (A)--(B) node[midway,above] {$a$};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,right] {$b$};
\path (C)--(D) node[midway,right] {$a$};
\path (D)--(E) node[midway,below] {$b$};
\path (E)--(F) node[midway,left] {$a$};
\path (F)--(A) node[midway,left] {$b$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
$\begin{align*}P&=3a+3b\\42&=3a+3(5)\\42&=3a+15\\27&=3a\\a&=9\text{ cm}\end{align*}$
Subtract $15$, then divide by $3$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (A) at (-1.2,1.1);
\coordinate (B) at (1.2,1.1);
\coordinate (C) at (1.9,0);
\coordinate (D) at (0.9,-1.6);
\coordinate (E) at (-0.9,-1.6);
\coordinate (F) at (-1.9,0);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--(E)--(F)--cycle;
\path (A)--(B) node[midway,above,text={rgb,255:red,38;green,140;blue,255}] {$9\text{ cm}$};
\path (B)--(C) node[midway,right] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\path (C)--(D) node[midway,right,text={rgb,255:red,38;green,140;blue,255}] {$9\text{ cm}$};
\path (D)--(E) node[midway,below] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\path (E)--(F) node[midway,left,text={rgb,255:red,38;green,140;blue,255}] {$9\text{ cm}$};
\path (F)--(A) node[midway,left] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
